{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_136","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text())\nr['testingFeedback']=['10 unique issues caught and fixed; details and confirming checks are recorded in docs/issues.md.','5 critical issues: a boot syntax error, blocked grand-course progress, dropped same-tick finish, unbounded direct disconnect, and shared-keyboard seat aliases.','The complete input-driven 11-stop tour and all 25 course/car legal-lap combinations; together they exposed progress and passport failures that smoke tests missed.','The cold-boot smoke check was useful but too narrow to reveal later route, menu, input, and connection failures.']\nr['engineFeedback']=['Native code-drawn shapes, E.Car, deterministic 120 Hz headless advance, and the controller-aware E.Shell made a coherent foundation.','The car brake could reverse from rest, and restoring a solo input preset after seat assignment reintroduced both players’ arrow aliases. Explicit adapters and tests resolved both.','A directed-gate route tracker and one host-authoritative pursuit simulation reused by local, WebRTC and Hub play.','Integrating native Shell pause/focus with live online menus and a match clock that works in an actorless server copy.','No upstream engine modifications. Game adapters use reverse:0, freeze grids, preserve analog intents, arbitrate pursuit incidents, and separate coincident cars before native contact.','Add a native directed-gate race-progress helper that handles shared roads, recovery anchors and ordered crossings.']\nr['promptFeedback']=['The source identity, exact hand-in naming, single-file requirement, and explicit hardware stand-ins made the delivery concrete.','PLAN.md specifies ultra effort while TASK.md specifies max. TASK.md was used for filenames and model metadata.','Completing controller/touch UX, legal route tracking and three multiplayer paths around one consistent simulation.','Keep a short mandatory acceptance checklist beside the delivery contract, with implementation suggestions and pacing targets separate.']\nr['sourceInformation']['online']='Shared-world host-authoritative AI Hub duels; standalone manual offer/answer WebRTC with matched motors; couch shared-keyboard, pad+keyboard and two-pad duels; AI opponent. Two local browser contexts and the official Hub harness are the permitted stand-ins. Cross-NAT internet, TURN and real remote-device connectivity: unknown.'\nr['sourceInformation']['animation']='Native shape groups, tweens, particles and Humanoid rigs; steering wheels, suspension, driver lean, pit-crew reactions, windmill sails, skids, dust, impact stars and splash rings.'\nr['sourceInformation']['testing']='Unlimited headless/state checks behind node tools/test.mjs; input-driven full tour, 2/5-lap trials, all course/car laps, controller/touch stand-ins, audio offline/analyser checks, real local WebRTC channels, and official Hub scenarios with 150 ms latency / 50 ms jitter / 5% loss; no FPS target.'\np.write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('../PROGRESS.md');s=p.read_text()+'\\\\n## Pre-final verification status\\\\n- Full browser UI/tour/input/touch suite reached 70 checks, with only a narrow single-window music-analyser sample failing; sample window is now broadened to cover rests.\\\\n- Four official Hub conformance scenarios passed (__hubCheck.pass true): one player, two players with latency/jitter/loss, host leave, actorless server.\\\\n- Direct real WebRTC match, lead/crash scoring, live menu, read-only diagnostics, final result, rematch and host closure: 14 checks passed. Added transport delay/loss tests for final pass.\\\\n- Phone Chromium and tablet WebKit: 8 checks passed. Shared-keyboard: 4 checks passed after preserving native half maps.\\\\n- 10 unique game issues fixed in docs/issues.md; 5 critical. Updated root exit-interview.json feedback, must verify final counts against any new issues.\\\\n- Added native crew/driver animation, remote render interpolation, stronger snapshot/ghost validation, and data-only sixth-course support.\\\\n- Formatted JS/CSS with Biome and Python with Ruff. Biome errors fixed; Python harness catch/loop warnings being cleaned.\\\\n- Next: final comprehensive node tools/test.mjs all; repair any failures, record evidence, inspect final screenshots/filmstrip, verify final HTML/report packaging. No persistent server or browser outside test commands.\\\\n';p.write_text(s)\nPY\nruff check --fix tests/browser.py > docs/evidence/ruff.log 2>&1\nruff format tests/browser.py > /dev/null\nbiome check --write src tools tests/*.mjs --diagnostic-level=error --max-diagnostics=20 > docs/evidence/biome.log 2>&1\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnode tools/test.mjs all\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_137","type":"agent_message","text":"The known failures are fixed. I’m running the comprehensive check on the bundled HTML: all car/course laps, the full tour, classic five-lap play, input and touch controls, audio, couch seats, WebRTC from file and loopback URLs, and Hub conformance. This pass also checks the report JSON and that the embedded Hub client remains unchanged.\n"}}
