{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_168","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/evidence/deliverable.json && tail -10 docs/issues.md && ls -lh ../*.html ../exit-interview.json ../PROGRESS.md'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"filename\": \"Auto-Motley-Motor-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-041247.html\",\n  \"bytes\": 1462954,\n  \"sha256\": \"3bff322a4e501a0e5077be75de37b6cddeb0d28a9e0cc49c36b237aec921d9c1\",\n  \"reportSha256\": \"02066ab3969b0a98e6a5b1055909beb8041e05d21d0d37f3cbf2c0bbee05e459\",\n  \"fullIntegration\": 171,\n  \"fullIntegrationFailures\": 0\n}\n| I04 | Critical (grand course progress) | Clean AI lap matrix after replacing overlapping grand-road curves | Reused exact base-road edge samples; allowed a car-width projection transition at corners while retaining local edge continuity and directed physical gates. | All five grand-course car profiles finish cleanly; no illegal projection transitions. |\n| I05 | Medium (tour passport) | Complete input-driven 11-stop tour | Require the discovery radius before ending the exploration stage. | Full tour completes with the forest stamp. |\n| I06 | Critical (online completion) | Same-tick authoritative finish regression | Order same-tick rule updates by authoritative event ID; reject duplicate/stale events. | Core regression and complete direct match/rematch pass. |\n| I07 | Medium (touch layout) | Phone landscape setup button interaction | Bounded setup minimum height to viewport so native panel scrolling can reach Start. | Phone Chromium and tablet WebKit multitouch, pause/resume and rendering pass. |\n| I08 | Medium (online menu) | Real two-context WebRTC match and Escape | Consume the opening Escape so native Shell does not also interpret it as Back on that tick. | Real-channel menu, diagnostics, complete scored match and rematch pass. |\n| I09 | Critical (online disconnect) | Real host page closure after rematch | Added explicit pagehide channel close and an 8-second application liveness deadline; finished peers continue compact heartbeats until rematch/leave. | Real host closure ends guest cleanly within the deadline; 14 direct checks pass. |\n| I10 | Critical (couch seats) | Shared-keyboard steering/braking separation | Reapplied native per-seat half-keyboard maps after setup instead of the solo aliases; preserved Enter for menus. | Shared-keyboard independent steering, braking and pause pass. |\n| I11 | Medium (AI traffic) | Complete scored couch duels with two emulated drivers | Gave two-car AI route-aware opposing lanes so a faster motor can pass instead of following a center-line queue into a scoreless draw. | Core AI passing regression and both controller-seat scored-duel checks pass. |\n| I12 | Medium (gate contact) | Contact-push gate regression | Retained the prior authoritative motion point so a physical push across a gate is observed on the next tick; reset anchors clear that history. | 32 core checks and the full 171-check integration suite pass. |\n| I13 | Low (TV preview) | Final 1920×1080 setup still | Added vertical room to keep the third car-comparison bar visible while preserving phone viewport bounds. | Final 1920×1080 still shows speed, pickup and cornering bars together. |\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1.4M Nov  6 05:47 ../Auto-Motley-Motor-Auto-Racing-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-041247.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 6.8K Nov  6 05:47 ../PROGRESS.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 4.8K Nov  6 05:41 ../exit-interview.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_169","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\ncfg=json.loads(Path('build-config.json').read_text());html=Path('../'+cfg['stem']+'.html');digest=hashlib.sha256(html.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\nproof=json.loads(Path('docs/evidence/deliverable.json').read_text());assert digest==proof['sha256'];assert html.read_bytes()==Path('index.html').read_bytes()\nfull=json.loads(Path('docs/evidence/tests-all.json').read_text());assert full['failed']==0\nhub=[json.loads(p.read_text()) for p in Path('docs/evidence').glob('hub-*.json')];assert len(hub)==4 and all(r['pass'] for r in hub)\ninterview=json.loads(Path('../exit-interview.json').read_text());assert '13 unique' in interview['testingFeedback'][0]\nPath('docs/validation.md').write_text('''# Validation evidence\n\nThe delivered game is complete. The full core/integration run passed 171 checks with zero failures. Final packaging passed 8 checks, final visual capture passed 2 checks, and all four official Hub scenarios passed again after the final Hub status-control adjustment.\n\n## Behaviour exercised\n\n- All 25 course/car combinations finish valid, clean AI laps using the real car model and ordered directed gates.\n- Input-driven title → all eleven tour stops → ending → replay, including a real splash/recovery, the inter-course connection, both pursuit scoring rules, a complete Duel, and the grand lap.\n- Two-lap and classic five-lap trials, split timing, recovery penalties, versioned best/ghost data, retries, pause, dev tuning/reset, record separation, storage failure and malformed ghost fallback.\n- Forward gates and rejection of reversed/skipped/teleported/oscillating line attempts, nearby-road continuity, safe restart slots, simultaneous crashes, crash-over-lead priority, wins, draws and same-tick final state delivery. Contact-pushed gate crossings have a regression check.\n- Shared-keyboard independent seats, pad+keyboard and two-pad seat assignment, complete scored couch duels, analog triggers, controller disconnect safety, native focus and glyph settings.\n- Chromium phone and WebKit tablet touch stand-ins: simultaneous steering/braking, interruption cleanup, pause/resume and native rendering.\n- Ten-second attract boundary, immediate consumed exit, and no passport/record writes.\n- The hidden airfield straight starts and finishes a real timed driving run. A native headless drawing pass completes without errors.\n- Offline synthesized motor/SFX/voice signal is nonzero and bounded; live procedural music is measured across note/rest windows; initial music gain is .10 and master mute reaches zero.\n- Real WebRTC channels in separate browser contexts, from file URLs and a loopback URL: gathered invitation/reply candidates, malformed input, readiness, matched cars, authoritative lead/crash points, live menu, read-only diagnostics, finish, rematch and vanished-host cleanup. Application-level 150 ms delay and 5% state loss are applied around the actual channels.\n- Official Hub harness: one player, two players with 150 ms latency / 50 ms jitter / 5% loss, host departure, and actorless server authority. Every report has pass=true, not just completion=true. Forbidden side-transport constructors are guarded in these tests.\n- The final HTML has no external scripts or audio/image-file dependencies. Its first script is byte-for-byte the pinned official Hub client. Engine notices and full MIT license are included. Root and development HTML match; exit-interview.json has the required schema and matches the in-game report.\n\n## Inspectable artifacts\n\n- tests-all.json, tests-core.json, tests-package.json, tests-visual.json and tests-hub.json: quiet-run results.\n- ai-laps.json and tour-playthrough.json: actual simulation outcomes.\n- direct-file.json and direct-loopback.json: real two-context final match states and ICE-candidate counts.\n- hub-standard-1.json, hub-standard-2.json, hub-host-leave-2.json, hub-server-2.json: official checker reports.\n- title-final.png, setup-final.png, driving.png, results.png, about.png, dev.png, phone.png, tablet-webkit.png, tour-ending.png: composition/input evidence.\n- filmstrip.png and motion.json: real steering, skid and brake poses with moving camera/scenery. Reviewed visually.\n- deliverable.json: final byte count and SHA-256 digests.\n\nAll evidence files are in docs/evidence. docs/issues.md tracks 13 unique issues, including 5 critical issues, their fixes and confirming checks. Earlier failure logs remain as history; the named final result files take precedence.\n\n## Practical limits\n\nPhysical controllers, real touch hardware, a TV, real iOS Safari, human listening, external remote-device play, cross-NAT internet and TURN coverage are unknown. Testing used the explicitly permitted stand-ins. Chromium and WebKit were exercised; Firefox was not part of this validation run. No FPS target, profiling or optimization gate was imposed. Tests close their own browsers and loopback servers; none remain running for this build.\n''')\nPath('../PROGRESS.md').write_text(f'''# Auto Motley Motor — complete\n\n## Deliverables\n- Game: \"'`{cfg['\"'stem']}.html\"'` in this workspace root; {len(html.read_bytes()):,} bytes, self-contained.\n- Reporting: `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML; exact required schema, embedded in the game’s paged About/Credits.\n- Development: `{cfg['\"'stem']}/\"'` contains sources, pinned vendor references, build/test tools, docs and evidence.\n- SHA-256: `{digest}`.\n\n## Verification\n- Full core/integration suite: **171 checks, 0 failures**.\n- Final packaging: **8 checks, 0 failures**. Final visual capture: **2 checks, 0 failures**.\n- All **4 official Hub conformance scenarios pass**, including latency/loss, host leave and actorless server. Final Hub rerun passed after the last UI polish.\n- Legal AI laps on all 25 course/car combinations; full input-driven eleven-stop tour and ending; classic five-lap trial; complete scored AI/couch/direct duels and rematches.\n- Shared keyboard, pad+keys, two pads, analog triggers, controller-loss safety, Chromium phone and WebKit tablet touch stand-ins.\n- Real WebRTC from file and loopback URLs; host loss, readiness, scoring, result/rematch, 150 ms application delay and 5% state loss.\n- Code-only audio measured offline/live, music .10, mute; attract boundary/no saves; dev/reset/unranked records; corrupt storage/ghost handling; final single-file packaging and report schema.\n- Native headless rendering and hidden straight timing pass. Final TV setup still and four-frame steering/skid/braking filmstrip inspected.\n- **13 unique issues fixed; 5 critical.** See development docs/issues.md and docs/validation.md. No required work remains.\n\n## Architecture for later work\n- Full my-3D2dge 0.89.1 pinned at 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691, unchanged upstream engine. vendor/engine links to the pinned sparse handoff.\n- Official AI Hub client 1.4.0 / protocol 1 pinned at 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869, inlined unmodified first after charset. vendor/hub includes harness/bridge/round support.\n- src/data.js, world.js, sim.js, storage.js, art.js, audio.js, net.js, ui.js, main.js and style.css. Plain modules bundled into a single HTML by tools/build.mjs.\n- Simulation alone advances each E.Car once per 1/120-second step; E.Race.update is not used. reverse:0, frozen grids, directed gates, retained contact motion, incident arbitration, safe anchors, one shared authority model.\n- Native E.Shell, shapes, materials, rigs, pixels, tweens, particles and audio buses are the presentation foundation.\n- Network uses a Worker-backed monotonic scheduler, Hub timeline/transport or standalone RTC. Actor identity is separate from authority. Online balance tools are read-only.\n- All five connected original courses and five motors/four profiles work. Time trial 2/5 laps, guided tour, AI/couch/RTC/Hub pursuit, free drive/passport/hidden timed airfield, personal ghosts, dev tools, settings and ten-second attract are implemented.\n- Title was chosen using Python secrets.randbelow(50) from fifty private candidates; method/index retained in development build-config.json.\n\n## Commands\nRun from the development folder:\n- `node tools/build.mjs` rebuilds both development index.html and the root deliverable, embedding the current root exit interview.\n- `node tools/test.mjs all` is the quiet test entry. Filters include core, sim, grand, package, browser, tour, input, couch, seats, touch, audio, direct, loopback, hub and visual.\n- Documentation: docs/research.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/authoring.md, docs/validation.md. Evidence: docs/evidence/.\n\n## Limits and environment\nCross-NAT/TURN internet, real remote devices, physical pads/touch/TV, real iOS and listening remain unknown; permitted stand-ins were tested. No persistent servers or browser processes remain. All generated files stay in this workspace/development folder. No sibling projects or pre-existing parent git changes were modified. Usage is exactly “added on import”; no cost/token/time estimate is made.\n'\"''')\nprint('Delivery, report, hashes and progress verified.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
